---
source: crates/biome_html_analyze/tests/spec_tests.rs
expression: invalid.svelte
---
# Input
```svelte
<a href="/foo">Click me!</a>
<a href="foo">Click me!</a>
<a href="">Click me!</a>
<a href={"/foo"}>Click me!</a>
<a href={'/foo'}>Click me!</a>
<a href="/posts/{id}">Click me!</a>
<a href="{'/foo'}">Click me!</a>
<a href="/foo" rel="noopener">Click me!</a>
<a href="/foo" rel="">Click me!</a>
<a HREF="/foo">Click me!</a>
<a href="/foo" />

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid.svelte:1:4 lint/nursery/useSvelteKitResolve ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  i This link's href isn't built with resolve().
  
  > 1 │ <a href="/foo">Click me!</a>
      │    ^^^^^^^^^^^
    2 │ <a href="foo">Click me!</a>
    3 │ <a href="">Click me!</a>
  
  i Paths that aren't built with resolve() lack the app's base path, and SvelteKit can't check them against the app's routes.
  
  i Wrap the path in resolve() from $app/paths. If the link leaves the app, add rel="external".
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

```

